{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>For one moment I would go up in your midst and consume you.</b> You mourn over what I said, 'For I will not go up in your midst' — yet this is indeed good for you, for if I were to go up in your midst I would consume you, since you are a stiff-necked people that does not turn to heed the voice of reprovers, while you are nonetheless prepared for perfection through a spiritual disposition acquired at the stand at Mount Sinai." "<b>And now, remove your ornament from upon you.</b> That spiritual preparation given to you at that august event — remove it from upon you. For the blessed El, after He has given a gift, does not take it back from the recipient without the recipient's consent, as they said, of blessed memory (Ta'anit 25a): דִּגְמִירִי דְּמִיהַב יְהַבֵי מַשְׁקְלֵי לָא שָׁקְלֵי (it is known that one who gives, gives; He does not take back)." "<b>And I will know what to do to you.</b> So that you will not then be deserving of so great a punishment."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:53.192471796Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}